BASED ON NEXOPP — ATTRIBUTION AND MODIFICATION NOTICE
===============================================================================

This program is a derivative of **NeXopp**, the Android `.xopp` editor written by
Brian Monroe (bamonroe):

    NeXopp — https://github.com/bamonroe/NeXopp
    Copyright (C) Brian Monroe.
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.

The whole application skeleton comes from that project: the `.xopp` reader/writer and the
dependency-free XML layer, the Compose editor, the drawing surface and input pipeline, the tab/
split-view/pane plumbing, the audio sidecar, the SAF open/save paths, the build and test tooling,
and the documentation structure. This project is a continuation of that codebase under new
ownership and the new name MobiXournal, so the work as a whole
remains under the copyright of its original author and the terms of the GPL-2.0-or-later.

CHANGES relative to NeXopp (measured against upstream's master head, file by file, after
normalising the package name: 287 shared source files, 21 added, 33 removed, 283 of the shared
ones modified):

  1. The radial palette was deleted outright - 33 files: its renderer, tap detector, haptics,
     action/catalog/editor/list/manager/reset components, its codec/hit-test/label/layout files and
     all of their tests.
  2. Its settings section "Palette" became "Shortcuts": one configurable key per tool and per pen
     colour, plus the pen/eraser and hand/pan toggles (AppSettings.toolShortcutKeys and
     colorShortcutKeys). NeXopp had no keyboard shortcuts at all.
  3. The rail was regrouped from eight slots to twelve: pen and highlighter separated, Line and
     Rectangle given slots of their own, the other figures sharing a Shapes slot, and text
     authoring split out of Insert (ToolGroups.kt).
  4. The shape recogniser was replaced with a direct port of desktop Xournal++'s (new Inertia.kt,
     RecoSegment.kt, CircleRecognizer.kt and a rewritten ShapeRecognizer.kt), supplanting a
     hand-rolled classifier.
  5. Colours were re-derived from desktop Xournal++: its default palette hex for hex,
     plus an HSV/hex custom slot (NeXopp shipped six hand-picked swatches),
     pinned by PaletteColorsTest. A recents row shipped with that round and has since been removed
     (see 14).
  6. The highlighter now blends with a separable BlendMode.MULTIPLY at 0.47 opacity on opaque
     paper, with the alpha-0x7f desktop store behaviour, and its tips snap to desktop Xournal++'
     2.83 / 8.50 / 19.84 pt sizes. NeXopp had neither the blend nor the tip sizes.
  7. Pen input gained a vendor-key barrel-button gate (the Honor Choice Pencil sends its side
     button as keyboard key 755), collapsing of that firmware's double-click into one action, a
     live Pen diagnostics log, and a whole-stroke eraser as the toggle's default.
  8. New affordances: a zoom badge above the page counter, a chevron on rail slots that open a
     submenu, a default page size setting, and a default-page-size tab in the page-size dialog.
  9. Saved files are announced as a real type - application/x-xopp with intent filters so the app
     shows up in Open with / Share sheets - where NeXopp wrote application/octet-stream; Save and
     the PDF export propose the document's own name.
 10. New identity and artwork: the name MobiXournal, applicationId and namespace com.mobixournal
     (NeXopp used com.nexopp for both), creator="MobiXournal" (NeXopp wrote "NeXopp"), this
     project's own sheet-and-pencil launcher icon with an Android 13+ monochrome layer, AGENTS.md
     in place of CLAUDE.md, and credits to NeXopp and Xournal++ in place of the Patreon link.
 11. Earlier update round (the work that led to this continuation), carried forward and kept:
     the highlighter opens on its own defaults - the palette's yellow at the thickest tip - and
     keeps a colour and width independent of the pen's (AppSettings.DEFAULT_HIGHLIGHTER_COLOR /
     DEFAULT_HIGHLIGHTER_WIDTH, EditorUiState.highlighterColor / highlighterWidth); large,
     Xournal++-authored .xopp files no longer lag when scrolling or writing, because a pressure
     stroke is now painted as one filled outline built in a single pass instead of one drawLine
     per segment - and the outline keeps the stroke's real per-point width, so the taper shows as
     it does on the desktop (StrokePainter.drawPressureLine); the pen gained the desktop's
     pressure settings, matching the desktop exactly (a Pressure sensitivity switch, a minimum
     pressure floor and a pressure multiplier, so the same press stores the same width as
     PenInputHandler::filterPressure), and the line/shape tools draw at the size setting verbatim so
     a shape and a pen stroke look the same in both apps; and the keyboard shortcuts (pen/eraser and
     hand/pan toggles, one key per tool and per pen colour - black, red and green pen and the
     highlighter) are read from the native dispatchKeyEvent rather than a Compose onKeyEvent, so
     any character works, upper or lower case.
 12. New in this continuation: the shape tools gained the STEM figures - Triangle, Square, Rhombus,
     Pentagon, Hexagon and Star (ShapeKind / ShapeBuilder.kt); line style (Solid/Dashed/Dash-dot/
     Dotted) moved into the Colour & size pop-up, so the pen can be dashed without leaving it, as
     the line style sits in the desktop's pen options; and a new Figures
     settings section sets the default figure size (which of the pen's S/M/L slots a new figure
     starts at) and reorders / hides the Shapes submenu (AppSettings.shapeOrder / shapeHidden). The
     default figure size is the knob for the pressure gap: a figure draws at its full set width
     while a pen stroke thins with pressure, so with Pressure sensitivity on a figure can look
     thicker than a light pen stroke.
 13. New in this continuation: the Colour & size pop-up was made compact (swatches in a tight grid,
     the three tip sizes as one bar, line style as a row of chips) and is
     now the *only* home of line style - the separate Style rail slot was removed, so it
     costs one rail button instead of two (RailItems.kt, ToolbarSizePopup.WidthSlotBar,
     ToolbarStylePopup.LineStyleChips). The pen palette became editable under a new Colors settings
     section: add, redefine and delete swatches (AppSettings.penColors, seeded with PEN_COLORS and
     capped at MAX_PEN_COLORS); the last
     colour cannot be deleted and deleting one drops its keyboard shortcut too. The Rhombus tool
     now draws its own hollow-rhombus glyph rather than Material's filled Diamond, so it reads as an
     outline like Square, Rectangle, Pentagon and Hexagon (ToolGlyphs.kt).
 14. New in this continuation: the shipping palette is now eight swatches - Black,
     Red, Green, Blue, Orange, Magenta, Yellow, White, in that order, each hex still Xournal++'s own
     for that colour (PEN_COLORS, pinned by PaletteColorsTest) - and the recently-used "Recent" row and its
     persisted list (recentColors / MAX_RECENT_COLORS / withColorUsed's MRU half) are gone: the
     palette is the list. Fill is removed from the app entirely (no control, no fillEnabled /
     fillAlpha / currentFill), so strokes drawn here are never flooded; the .xopp `fill` attribute
     is still read, rendered and written, so a document that already carries it round-trips
     untouched. The three size boxes in the pop-up were tightened (smaller dot box, less padding),
     and WidthDot's minimum dot is now a fraction of its box rather than a fixed 23dp offset, so a
     smaller box can't end up with a floor wider than itself.
 15. New in this continuation: the rail's Shape recognition and Guides slots no longer share one
     glyph. Shape recognition carries a magic wand (AutoFixHigh) instead of the triangle it had in
     common with the Triangle *tool* - which is why it read as "draw a triangle" rather than "tidy
     up what I drew" - and Guides carries a ruler (Straighten), the one pictogram that already means
     "rule a straight line" (ToolbarStylePopup.kt, ToolbarViewPopups.kt). Both new faces come from
     material-icons-extended, already a dependency. The pen and the figure tools now default to the
     **middle** pen-width slot (DEFAULT_SHAPE_WIDTH / DEFAULT_SHAPE_SLOT moved from index 2 to 1,
     matching lastWidth): a figure is drawn at its width with no pressure, so starting it at the top
     slot made a fresh shape visibly fatter than fresh handwriting. The highlighter keeps the wide
     slot, since it lays a band rather than a stroke. Finally the palette keeps the user's own
     colours: sanitized() and decodePenColors no longer prune anything absent from
     PREDEFINED_COLOR_NAMES, so a swatch added under Settings -> Colors survives a restart and is
     carried in - and restored from - the JSON backup, which already serialised penColors. That
     name table is now display-only, and the eight shipping swatches remain desktop Xournal++'s own
     hexes, pinned by DesktopColorParityTest against upstream palettes/xournal.gpl.

Substantial portions are unchanged: the .xopp reader/writer and the dependency-free XML layer,
the Compose editor, the drawing surface and input pipeline, the tabs/panes/audio plumbing, the
SAF open/save paths, the build and test tooling, and the documentation structure.

